title: Make the experimental collator proto the default for Kusama
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    The binary checks if a Kusama chainspec is loaded and enables the experimental collator protocol by default unless
    `experimental-collator-protocol` parameter is passed explicitly. In that case its value is respected no matter what the chainspec is.

    The change reworks the `experimental-collator-protocol` to accept an optional true/false value in the format
    `--experimental-collator-protocol=[true|false]'. In practice this means there are there are a few cases:
    - no `experimental-collator-protocol` parameter is provided -> experimental is enabled for Kusama and disabled for any other chainspec.
    - `experimental-collator-protocol=true` or `experimental-collator-protocol=false` -> experimental is explicitly enabled or disabled no matter what the chain spec is.
    - `--experimental-collator-protocol` is provided without any value (the same as `--experimental-collator-protocol=true`) experimental is enabled no matter what the chain spec is.
crates:
- name: polkadot-cli
  bump: patch
